The price-to-earnings ratio, or P/E ratio, is a common valuation metric that compares a company's current stock price to its earnings per share (EPS) over a specific period of time, typically a year. A higher P/E ratio generally indicates that investors are expecting strong future growth from the company, while a lower ratio may suggest that the market has low expectations or that the stock is undervalued.
